.TH EARTHVIEW-WALLPAPER 1 "August 2026" "2.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
earthview\-wallpaper \- multi\-source desktop wallpaper engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B earthview\-wallpaper
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B earthview\-wallpaper
runs a system tray indicator that sets the desktop wallpaper from satellite
and photographic imagery fetched from several providers.
.PP
Only one instance runs at a time. Starting a second one exits immediately
rather than adding a duplicate tray icon.
.SH SOURCES
.TP
.B Google Earth View
Curated satellite landscapes. Bundled locally, no network index required.
.TP
.B NASA EPIC
Full\-disc Earth from the DSCOVR satellite, drawn from the full archive.
.TP
.B Himawari\-8
Japan Meteorological Agency imagery, updated every ten minutes.
.TP
.B GOES\-19 / GOES\-18
NOAA GeoColor composites covering the Americas, full disc and regional.
.TP
.B NASA APOD
Astronomy Picture of the Day.
.TP
.B Unsplash
Scenery, aerial, and space photography.
.SH MODES
.TP
.B Random
Sources are used in strict rotation so each is selected in turn.
.TP
.B Locked
Restrict changes to one or more chosen sources via Lock to Sources in the tray
menu. Locked sources rotate evenly among themselves. Change From Source
ignores the lock, being an explicit one-off request.
.TP
.B Time\-aware
Selects imagery matching the current time of day.
.TP
.B Fly\-over
Advances along a scenic route, or shows imagery near your location.
.PP
No image repeats within seven days. Used URLs are recorded in
.IR ~/.config/earthview/recent_urls.json .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/earthview/config.json
Active sources, source lock, interval, and mode settings.
.TP
.I ~/.config/earthview/history.json
Recently applied wallpapers.
.TP
.I ~/.config/earthview/favorites.json
Saved favourites.
.TP
.I ~/.config/earthview/recent_urls.json
Deduplication record used to suppress repeats.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/earthview/wallpaper.jpg
The currently applied wallpaper image.
.TP
.I ~/.config/earthview/collections/
User\-supplied collections, loaded alongside the bundled ones.
.SH NOTES
NASA APOD uses a shared demo key by default and is rate limited to roughly
thirty requests per hour. Supply a personal key from
.UR https://api.nasa.gov
.UE
under Preferences, Sources for reliable access. Unsplash works without a key.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gsettings (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Alper Sakarya and contributors.
